      "claim": "Volcanic emissions, especially submarine volcanism and hydrothermal vents, introduce dissolved gases and ions (e.g., Cl⁻, SO₄²⁻, Fe²⁺) into seawater.",
      "evidence": "Measurements of vent fluids at mid‑ocean ridges show concentrations of Cl⁻ comparable to seawater and elevated SO₄²⁻, indicating a net addition of salts (German & Seyfried, 2014).",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": []
    },
