      "id": 3,
      "claim": "Reactions on the sea floor, such as dissolution of basaltic crust and hydrothermal circulation, release additional mineral ions into the ocean.",
      "evidence": "Hydrothermal flux estimates indicate ~0.1 Tmol yr⁻¹ of Mg²⁺ and other cations are added to the ocean from seafloor alteration (Alt & Karstensen, 1999).",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": []
    },
